; An active region is the range, and its end follows the replacements.
> (define b (show "r" "a a a a a\n"))
> (views:set-mark! (view) 3)
> (views:set-point! (view) 8)
> (replace! "M-%" "a" "xyz")
> (list (asked) (views:mark (view)))
> (press! "!")
> (text)
((4 "Query replacing a with xyz: (? for help) " "a") #f)
"a xyz xyz xyz a\n"
; A match crossing the range's end is cut there, and the pattern sees the
; view's bounds, as in Emacs: a+ over the first two characters of aaaa
; gives baa; \bfoo\b and C-u M-% foo over a region ending after foo in
; foobar replace nothing.
> (define c (show "c" "aaaa\n"))
> (views:set-mark! (view) 1)
> (views:set-point! (view) 3)
> (replace! "C-M-%" "a+" "b")
> (press! "!")
> (text)
> (define d (show "d" "foobar\n"))
> (views:set-mark! (view) 1)
> (views:set-point! (view) 4)
> (replace! "C-M-%" "\\bfoo\\b" "baz")
> (list (session) (text) (last-message))
> (views:set-mark! (view) 1)
> (views:set-point! (view) 4)
> (start! "C-u" "M-%")
> (type! "foo")
> (press! "RET")
> (sleep-for 0.05)
> (type! "baz")
> (press! "RET")
> (sleep-for 0.05)
> (list (session) (text) (last-message))
"baa\n"
(#f "foobar\n" "Replaced 0 occurrences")
(#f "foobar\n" "Replaced 0 occurrences")
; C-u M-% user and C-M-% \buser\b agree on user_id in fundamental, where
; _ is not a word character.
> (define u (show "u" "user_id user\n"))
> (start! "C-u" "M-%")
> (type! "user")
> (press! "RET")
> (sleep-for 0.05)
> (type! "uid")
> (press! "RET")
> (sleep-for 0.05)
> (press! "!")
> (text)
> (define u2 (show "u2" "user_id user\n"))
> (replace! "C-M-%" "\\buser\\b" "uid")
> (press! "!")
> (text)
"uid_id uid\n"
"uid_id uid\n"
; ^ does not match at a region's start in mid-line.
> (define m (show "m" "xab ab\n"))
> (views:set-mark! (view) 2)
> (views:set-point! (view) 7)
> (replace! "C-M-%" "^ab" "Z")
> (list (session) (text) (last-message))
(#f "xab ab\n" "Replaced 0 occurrences")
; With several cursors that have regions, only matches inside a region
; are asked about; each region's end follows the replacements before it.
> (define s (show "s" "a a a a a a\n"))
> (views:set-mark! (view) 1)
> (views:set-point! (view) 4)
> (define c2 (views:add-cursor! (view) 8))
> (views:set-cursor! c2 12 8)
> (replace! "M-%" "a" "bb")
> (asked)
> (press! "!")
> (text)
(2 "Query replacing a with bb: (? for help) " "a")
"bb bb a a bb bb\n"
; The scan, the highlights and the count hold the matches the session asks
; about, and only those.
> (define t (show "t" "a a a a a\n"))
> (views:set-mark! (view) 3)
> (views:set-point! (view) 8)
> (replace! "M-%" "a" "b")
> (sleep-for 0.2)
> (let ([sc (replace:session-scan (session))]) (list (search:scan-count sc) (search:scan-done? sc)))
> (faced (html->string (views:draw (view) client)))
> (press! "q")
(3 #t)
(("replace.match" "a") ("match.other" "a") ("match.other" "a"))
